WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:07.730
I'm Will Lewis, I'm a Principal Program Manager
with the Microsoft Translator team.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:12.160
And recently we had a group of students who
were being hosted at the University of Washington,

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.500
a group of Chinese students in particular
Chinese undergraduate students,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.120
and they were visiting the University of Washington
for a few days.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.700
They brought them over here to MSR for a brief
time to introduce them to the research that

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.040
is being done at Microsoft Research.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:35.640
So we actually had them come to a talk that
I was giving on what we do - on speech translation.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.670
So the translator live feature is the feature
allows you to create what we call a virtual

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:45.969
room where people can have conversations in
multiple languages.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:51.370
So one of the ways we host this is through
PowerPoint - so using the Presentation Translator.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:56.559
So on the screen is part of this add-in and
actually shows a QR code that people can use

00:00:56.559 --> 00:00:58.729
to join from their own devices.

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:02.670
And so what happens is while I'm talking they
will see the transcripts on the screen, if

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.430
I choose to have them on the screen, and then
they will also see the transcripts on their

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:09.600
local devices in the language of choice.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.909
And so when I talk you hear the Mandarin actually
being spoken as I talk.

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:18.620
[Playback of Mandarin translation]

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:24.780
I can speak while showing a PowerPoint deck, and it will show the transcripts on the screen

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.260
at the same time will allow people to join
from their own devices.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.720
[Xiaodong speaking in Mandarin]

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:38.240
So when Xiaodong asked his question, you see
the transcript of what he's asking on the

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.240
screen in English not in Mandarin.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.689
The students were completely amazed by this
feature where they saw the transcripts of

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:48.609
me talking - they were showing up on the screen
- then they were seeing them on their own

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:49.609
devices.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:53.219
And then they were seeing them in Chinese
script as I was talking and then at one point

00:01:53.219 --> 00:01:59.979
I turned on the audio so they could hear the
Mandarin being spoken as I was speaking English.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:05.399
So this feature is particularly important
in the classroom because it allows teachers

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:11.840
or lecturers or whatever to give a talk or
give a discussion in the class in their native

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.840
language.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.290
So for students who are non-native speakers
who are maybe are recent immigrants or maybe

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.290
visiting here - maybe they're visiting scholars,
for instance - they don't know the language

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.480
well, they have access then to the content
that's being discussed because they could

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.209
see the transcripts in their own language.

